title: $:/plugins/rimir/outline/changelog
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

! Changelog

|!Version |!Date |!Changes |
|0.0.17 |2026-11-27 |Block types are tiddlers (tag `$:/tags/rimir/outline/BlockType`; built-ins as shadows, new "Quote block" `<<<`): other plugins add types, e.g. rimir/graphviz and rimir/mermaid. Typed blocks (`$$$type`) of registered types: menu, turn into, badge, edited without the `$$$` lines. Turn into: everything into everything (content of several lines not into headings or list items; a list item becomes a block by splitting its list). Insert before / after list items (a new first bullet). Alt-Enter in a new, empty editor picks its type. "Add to this item" on bullets: a diagram tiddler created on the first save and transcluded; a double-click edits a transcluded diagram in place. |
|0.0.16 |2026-11-27 |A selected transclusion (`{{…}}`, `<$transclude>`) gets an orange frame instead of the blue one. |
|0.0.15 |2026-11-26 |Outline is always there and idle until used: Ctrl-Click (Cmd-Click on Mac) on a block wakes it, Escape with nothing selected, a click outside the tiddler or closing it puts it back to sleep; a closed tiddler forgets its selection and an open edit. An idle tiddler does no outline work (no parsing, no stamps, no refresh work) and looks and clicks as without the plugin. The //outline// toolbar button and `$:/state/rimir/outline/on/<title>` are gone. New: setting //Enabled// (`$:/config/rimir/outline/enabled`), field `outline: no` to leave a tiddler out; other plugins' body templates now come first. |
|0.0.14 |2026-11-26 |Turn into: a heading turns into another heading level (only its `!`s change, its section keeps its levels). A double-click on another unit while editing saves the edited unit and opens the editor on the clicked one. |
|0.0.13 |2026-11-25 |Fix: the block menu opened at the top of the page on units whose first element is hidden (code blocks with a plugin that adds a hidden caption before them); the menu and scrolling now go by the first visible element. |
|0.0.12 |2026-11-25 |Keys: Ctrl-Enter in selection mode starts a new empty unit below the selection (an item on its level, else a paragraph). In the editor, Enter at the start of a filled item or paragraph opens an empty one above, Delete at the end of an item pulls the item below up, Alt-Enter turns the edited unit into another type, and Ctrl-Z / Ctrl-Y undo / redo the outline's last change (a split, merge or move) while nothing is typed. The block menu moves from Shift-Enter to Alt-Enter. Fix: an untouched editor of an item or heading counted as changed. |
|0.0.11 |2026-11-25 |Fix: the editor left out list markers and heading `!`s, but showed a code block's fence lines and the `>`s of a whole quote; it now shows only the content of those too (also `<<<` quotes), saving puts the markup back. |
|0.0.10 |2026-11-25 |Copy, cut and paste (Ctrl-C / Ctrl-X / Ctrl-V in selection mode) through the system clipboard: a unit with its subtree pastes formatted into e-mail or Jira (HTML), as wikitext into text fields, and into an outline with its levels adapted to the place; plain text from elsewhere pastes as wikitext. Cut does not ask, Ctrl-Z undoes it; a copy flashes the unit. An empty new list item shows its marker and takes Tab / Shift-Tab as its level. |
|0.0.9 |2026-11-23 |Fix: keys pressed right after the editor opened (Home, arrows) could be undone by the late caret-to-end move, so Enter then saved instead of splitting the item. |
|0.0.8 |2026-11-23 |Block menu: //Insert before// (e.g. a heading above a list, a paragraph or a lower heading). Alt-Up/Down across heading lines: a heading moves up over the blocks above it (they join its section) and down over a higher heading; a paragraph or list moves into the next section and out of its own. An empty tiddler shows a hint: Enter writes a first paragraph, Shift-Enter offers the block types. Fix: a heading or paragraph could not be turned into a bullet next to a list. |
|0.0.7 |2026-11-23 |Undo: Ctrl-Z takes back the last changes made in the outline (move, indent, delete, merge, split, conversion, saved edit), Ctrl-Y / Ctrl-Shift-Z redoes; the selection goes back too. A split, merge or editor move is one step. History per tiddler for the session in a temp tiddler, 20 steps (setting); dropped when the tiddler is changed elsewhere. |
|0.0.6 |2026-11-22 |Double-click edits a unit. Delete removes the selection with its subtree after a yes/no menu (a heading: with its section or just the heading); list items without sub-items go at once (setting, default on). In the editor, Enter in the middle of a list item splits it at the caret, Backspace at its start merges it into the item above (an empty item is deleted). The editor opens with the caret at the end instead of a selection. Transclusion marker more visible. |
|0.0.5 |2026-11-22 |Type badges: a small, faint label beside every unit (paragraph, h1–h6, code-block, bullet, numbered, bullet-list, quote, table, transclusion, ...) in a reserved column on the right, also on the editor field; nothing moves or grows. Setting: all (default), headings only, off. |
|0.0.4 |2026-11-22 |Key overview: `?` (any keyboard layout, or the ? button) shows all keys next to the outline, Escape closes it; new //keys// tab with the same table. Settings use TW's shortcut editor (press to record, platform variants), grouped. Up/Down treat a whole list as one block (Down from a selected list goes to the next block, Up from below selects the whole list); Ctrl-Up/Down step through every item. Fix: an outside change could steal the focus from the editor. |
|0.0.3 |2026-11-22 |Enter edits, Shift-Enter opens a block menu (insert a paragraph, heading, list, quote or code block after the selection, or turn it into another type; a bullet switches list type with its siblings). Compact one-line editor by default (full editor with toolbar as a setting); the editor shows content without list markers or heading prefixes; line breaks in bullets and headings are saved as `<br>`. In the editor: Ctrl-Up/Down move to the previous/next unit, Tab/Shift-Tab indent/promote and Alt-Up/Down move the edited unit and keep editing. Left/Right select parent / first child. A bullet with sub-items is framed around its own line only; no selection frames while editing. Fixes: gap below the edited bullet, Shift-Enter error in the compact field, focus lost after an outside change, code blocks of plugins that replace core widgets (e.g. a $codeblock override) were not selectable. |
|0.0.2 |2026-11-20 |Alt-Up/Down keeps a comment between two touching blocks (it was deleted) and sets it apart with blank lines; the line after the moved pair keeps its indentation. FAQ: refused moves. |
|0.0.1 |2026-11-20 |First version: per-tiddler outline mode (ViewToolbar toggle), unit selection, Alt-Up/Down move and Tab/Shift-Tab indent with subtrees, in-place editor (save, save and new, cancel, conflict handling), transclusion jump, configurable shortcuts. Wikitext only. Moves of touching blocks add a blank-line separator; a model guard refuses structural results that change the units; structural keys are blocked while editing and still act right after a write; a changed edit survives re-renders and closing the tiddler; same-tiddler field transclusions are not mapped; a typed item marker is not doubled. |
